  "posts": [
    {
      "text": "Get booking for Christmas Day",
      "date": "",
      "permalink": null,
      "hasVideo": false,
      "imageKeys": [
        "k2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "A celebration as personal as the memories you share. Whether looking out over the open sea or surrounded by garden blooms, we’re here to support you in saying goodbye their way.",
      "date": "",
      "permalink": null,
      "hasVideo": true,
      "imageKeys": [
        "k3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Mornings in Guernsey are a little bit different",
      "date": "",
      "permalink": "https://www.facebook.com/100064681869040/videos/pcb.1569374098561971/3273933832805528",
      "hasVideo": true,
      "imageKeys": []
    },
    {
      "text": "The sounds of an afternoon spent at Petit Bot\n\nSecluded and sheltered on the south coast, Petit Bot is a great spot for exploring at any tide height.\n At high tide Petit Bot has a pebbled shore, at low tide it turns into a lovely sandy beach. There are lots of coves and rock pools to enjoy. The ever changing shores is one of the most beautiful parts of the coastal beaches, so you’ll find somewhere new every time.\nPetit Bot is also home to a tearoom where you can enjoy Guernsey ice cream, drinks and snacks.\nAt the bay you’ll also find one of the 15 Loophole Towers that were built to defend the island in 1778-9. A free exhibition of its history is available in the tower too!\n You can also arrange kayak hire at the beach from Outdoor Guernsey to explore the beach and coastline even further.\n#ThatIslandFeeling See less",
      "date": "",
      "permalink": "https://www.facebook.com/100064681869040/videos/pcb.1579199307579450/1715216680198426",
      "hasVideo": true,
      "imageKeys": []
    },
    {
      "text": "Mornings in Guernsey are a little bit different\n\nSavour the sunrise (around 7am in October) at The Heart of La Vallette before warming up with a sauna at Hot Haus Guernsey and enjoying breakfast in St Peter Port with a view out across Herm and Sark.\nDespite the air temperature cooling down, the sea is still retaining some of its summer warmth. Expect a fresh dip with temperature around 16 degrees\n\nWould you spend your morning like this?\n#ThatIslandFeeling See less",
      "date": "",
      "permalink": "https://www.facebook.com/100064681869040/videos/pcb.1569374098561971/3273933832805528",
      "hasVideo": true,
      "imageKeys": []
    },
    {
      "text": "\"From Michelin-starred restaurants to seafood and produce sourced just metres away, the Islands of Guernsey are making an increasingly compelling case for a food-focused escape across the Channel this year.\nEating here [is] less about chasing reservations and more about discovering how an island’s landscape, producers and cooks inform one another.\"\nDelighted to see Guernsey's gastonomic scene highlighted in Foodism UK\n See less",
      "date": "",
      "permalink": null,
      "hasVideo": false,
      "imageKeys": []
    },
    {
      "text": "Would you like to learn about Guernsey's weaving, foraging and ormering history?\nFather-daughter duo Claire and Max Gaudion are running a special retreat in February 2027 where you will be tutored through traditional Guernsey ‘ponier à cou’ making, head on foraging tours and try a classic ormer dish.\nFind out all the details at https://www.guernseywillowbaskets.com/retreat See less",
      "date": "",
      "permalink": null,
      "hasVideo": false,
      "imageKeys": [
        "k4",
        "k5",
        "k6"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Guernsey\n\n\"Making the perfect crab roll using the best local ingredients 2 Frenchies crispy French bread\n\nGuernsey Dairy for the best butter\n in the world & our freshly picked chancre crab\n hope you enjoy\n.\"\nThank you Bernie for sending in this brilliant video, this just has to be the perfect roll!\n#MyGuernsey\n Bernie Le Gallais\n A1 Crab Supplies Guernsey See less",
      "date": "",
      "permalink": null,
      "hasVideo": true,
      "imageKeys": []
    },
    {
      "text": "Visit Guernsey has been named Destination Brand of the Year at the Travel Marketing Awards",
      "date": "",
      "permalink": null,
      "hasVideo": false,
      "imageKeys": []
    },
    {
      "text": "Guernsey\n\nJust 40 minutes from the UK\nMake the most of your summer holiday with a short hop over to our Islands.\nDon't forget that if you're arriving in the Channel Islands directly from the UK or the Republic of Ireland, you do not need a passport - just some form of photographic identification.\nSkip the airport queues, and start getting #ThatIslandFeeling See less",
      "date": "",
      "permalink": null,
      "hasVideo": false,
      "imageKeys": [
        "k7",
        "k8",
        "k9"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Visit Guernsey\n\nWith yoga retreats, sporting events, artistic workshops, concerts and more on offer, there's plenty to enjoy across our Islands this month.\nSee below the upcoming events our Islands have in store for you.\nThis month includes the Spring Walking Festival, Rendez-Vous Aux Jardins, Creative Sark, Guernsey Together Festival, History Tours and more\n See less",
      "date": "",
      "permalink": null,
      "hasVideo": false,
      "imageKeys": []
    },
    {
      "text": "Guernsey’s tourism industry doesn’t survive on ridiculously good looking scenery alone, you know?\nThere’s a whole production of people working behind the scenes to put on an almighty tourism performance.\nIn fact, Guernsey’s Net Promoter Score (a metric often used to understand guest satisfaction levels) recently reached 72, which is very, very high.\nThat means visitors rate the islands as a top notch holiday destination.\nSo it was easy for me to give the welcome speech at the ‘Islands of Guernsey Travel Trade Summit’.\n70 business partners from across the UK, Europe, and of course the Bailiwick, have come together for three days of forging partnerships and building on our tourism successes.\n“Guernsey is an incredible place to do business; not just because we are a world class finance centre; not just because we boast a spectacular seascape backdrop; but because our entire community is wide open and entirely\naccessible - to you.” See less",
      "date": "",
      "permalink": null,
      "hasVideo": false,
      "imageKeys": [
        "k10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "There are so many exciting events to explore at The Big Eat Food Festival\nMany are ones that you can attend whenever you visit in April, or take place every week. You'll also find special menus celebrating local produce at restaurants across Guernsey, Herm, Sark and Alderney\nSwipe to see what's on throughout April.\nBrowse all the festival activities and menus at https://thebigeatguernsey.com/ See less",
      "date": "",
      "permalink": null,
      "hasVideo": false,
      "imageKeys": [
        "k11",
        "k12",
        "k13",
        "k14",
        "k15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "With Balthazar Restaurant & Bar, Guernsey – I just got recognised as one of their top fans!",
      "date": "",
      "permalink": null,
      "hasVideo": true,
      "imageKeys": [
        "k16"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Sea swimming is a popular pastime on the Islands of Guernsey and is a great way to get active outdoors and see our coastline from an alternative perspective. Our waters are safe and, especially in the summer, provide a refreshing and rejuvenating experience.\n @luke_meller See less",
      "date": "",
      "permalink": null,
      "hasVideo": false,
      "imageKeys": [
        "k17"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "",
      "date": "",
      "permalink": null,
      "hasVideo": false,
      "imageKeys": [
        "k18"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "For Sale – Hardy Seawings 277 (1996)\n| £27,500 Ex Vat | Lying Guernsey\n2 x 205 hp Volvo Penta 4.3GS petrol engines, regularly serviced — last major engine & stern drive service: Sept 2023.\n Well-equipped for cruising\n• Electric anchor windlass\n• Radar / chartplotter\n• Depthsounder\n• VHF radio\n• TV/DVD player\n• Beaching legs\n• Tender with snap davits + electric outboard\n• Shorepower & battery charger\n Recent care: Hull antifouled & engines/stern drives checked July 2025\n Spacious, comfortable & ideal for family adventures\n Martin on 07781 104646 to arrange a viewing See less",
      "date": "",
      "permalink": null,
      "hasVideo": false,
      "imageKeys": [
        "k19"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Planning a visit to our Islands with your four-legged friend? Here's everything you need to know about travelling with a dog.\n Dogs are welcome on the cliff paths, at most al fresco dining locations and even some shops and cafes. You can find a range of pet-friendly accommodation across the islands, from campsites to five-star hotels.\n Most of the Islands’ beaches allow dogs to enjoy the space year-round, from 1st May to 30th September there are restrictions, but there is always a beach available for you all to enjoy.\n Pets visiting from the UK, other Channel Islands and the Isle of Man are generally able to visit without a Pet Passport.\n You can bring your pet to Guernsey on the ferry from the UK and France, operated by Brittany Ferries.\n If you are visiting with a guide dog, they will be welcome across the Islands.\nFor more information and guidance, head to: https://www.visitguernsey.com/.../visiting-with-your-pet/ See less",
      "date": "",
      "permalink": null,
      "hasVideo": false,
      "imageKeys": [
        "k20"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Mood because March has finally arrived\n @kristelaaslaid\n#ThatIslandFeeling See less",
      "date": "",
      "permalink": null,
      "hasVideo": false,
      "imageKeys": [
        "k21"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "",
      "date": "",
      "permalink": null,
      "hasVideo": false,
      "imageKeys": [
        "k22"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Did you know that forest bathing and time in nature can help reduce cortisol levels, allowing you to feel calmer and more peaceful?\nSometimes all you need is just space to walk, think and be.\nOur 2026 mantra: less grind, more ground. See less",
      "date": "",
      "permalink": null,
      "hasVideo": false,
      "imageKeys": [
        "k23"
      ]
    }
  ],
